  "reasoning": "The patient presents with calf cramps, difficulty walking, and fatigue after work, explicitly linking these issues to obesity. These symptoms are classic indicators of venous insufficiency, where increased abdominal pressure from excess weight strains the leg veins, causing blood pooling, cramping, and tiredness. Conditions like arthritis primarily involve joint inflammation and stiffness, while diabetes typically presents with metabolic symptoms such as excessive thirst and frequent urination. Since the clinical picture centers on lower limb discomfort and fatigue exacerbated by weight without joint or systemic metabolic complaints, varicose veins is the most factually supported diagnosis.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]varicose veins[/DIAGNOSIS]"
